"They say that people who are good at a game don't want to change it..."

This is not meant to be a flame, but come on, dave, would you please for
once not defend EVERY little aspect of NetHack that someone thinks is
wrong?  I agree that NetHack is a good game, but features tend to be added
very quickly, which can make it difficult to maintain realism and game
balance.  And yes, I also agree with you that 'realism' in a medevial
dungeon setting is somewhat oxymoronic, but that didn't stop Tolkein from
writing a series of very realistic medevial-type books, and it shouldn't
stop us from trying to make NetHack as realistic as possible.  Now, a
rust monster, realistically, should NOT effect magical bonuses.  It merely
rusts your armor, making it weaker.  I agree with Ofer (Ofer?) that it
doesn't make sense to have a rusted shield actually make you _easier_ to
hit.  I think having it crumble away would be much more 'realistic,' and
could even cause some really annoying problems (bye bye Mr. Shield of
Reflection).  

A side note: I've been away from the net for a while, and was wondering
what happened with the pool/floating eye confirmation debate.  I was
for having confirmation available because, again, realistically, you would
not intentionally attack a monster you didn't want to attack, or walk
into a pool that you didn't want to walk into.  Has anything been
changed in PL9 along these lines?
